# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Mutex with configurable queue depth (Mutex.new(0), Mutex.new(1), etc.);
#         'Mutex used as Tag' colon-scope notation; fairness and queue-overflow behavior.
# deferred: v1.x — Mutex stdlib type not in v1.0 scope
# matrix-row: stdlib-mutex
#
# Reason:
#   Mutex is a stdlib synchronization primitive scheduled for M6.  This variant
#   additionally tests the 'm:{ ... }' tag-scope notation with a Mutex (treating
#   Mutex as a Tag — requires Mutex to inherit from Tag, M4 prototype-OOP), and
#   uses 'for&(...)' parallel for loops (M5 chk driver).  Queue-depth testing
#   exercises the blocking acquire with bounded-wait semantics.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Mutex type and M5 chk driver):
# # var m = Mutex.new()|; var shared = ""|; var count = 0|;
# # function check(v = String.fresh()) { v }|; check() != check();
# # [00000001] true
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/mutex/queued.chk)
